# Java Backend — aCis Gameserver

## Ubicación
- `aCis_gameserver/java/net/sf/l2j/gameserver/` — todo el código del servidor

## Paquetes clave

| Paquete | Propósito |
|---|---|
| `phantom/` | Phantoms (bots): AI, combate, inventario, social, factories |
| `factionwar/` | Faction War Manager, Config, Checkpoints, Registry |
| `event/` | Sistema de eventos (TvT, DM, CTF, etc.) |
| `communitybbs/` | Community Board (Alt+B) |
| `model/actor/` | Clases base: Player, Creature, Npc, etc. |
| `handler/admincommandhandlers/` | Comandos admin (AdminPhantom, AdminFactionWar, etc.) |
| `data/xml/` | Cargadores de XML: FactionData, etc. |
| `network/clientpackets/` | Paquetes del cliente |
| `network/serverpackets/` | Paquetes al cliente |

## Cómo compilar
```bash
# Con Ant (build.xml)
ant -f aCis_gameserver/build.xml

# O manualmente con javac
cd aCis_gameserver
javac -encoding UTF-8 -source 21 -target 21 -cp "lib/*" -d build/classes -sourcepath java ruta/al/archivo.java
```

## Convenciones
- Java 21 (records, pattern matching, switch expressions)
- No usar Javolution ni librerías deprecadas
- Thread safety: usar `ConcurrentHashMap`, `volatile` para flags compartidos
- Logging: usar `CLogger` de `net.sf.l2j.commons.logging`
- Config: leer desde properties con `ExProperties`
- HTML en NPCs: usar `NpcHtmlMessage` con `setFile()` o `setHtml()`
